      "side": 1,
      "message": "`__pkvm_va` doesn\u0027t check the bounds for phys and we will have a problem if phys doesn\u0027t fit in the direct map window. If phys is greater than or equal to MAXMEM, __pkvm_va() returns a value greater than VMALLOC_START and pkvm_hyp_mmu_map() can collide with vmemmap or hypervisor .text/.data in hyp_mmu.\n\nWould it make sense to have a check to see if it fits in the direct map window before we acquire the mmu lock - something like:\n\n```\nif (phys + size \u003e MAXMEM)\n    return -EINVAL;\n```\n\nThis was an issue in iommu_init as well, but we trusted the host during initialization to not pass in a bad range for [iommu-\u003ereg, iommu-\u003ereg + size). Now that we are exposing this as an api, it would be safer to have the above check I guess.",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "a3f3cdde_7cb0cd67",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 1,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 1,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\tif (phys + size \u003e MAXMEM)\n\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "b8fe32b2de3ad8672a55cc43b1ec59491457588a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
